{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > tests/browser.py <<'PY'\nimport json\nimport pathlib\nimport sys\nfrom playwright.sync_api import sync_playwright\n\nroot = pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]\nurl = (root / 'build/game.html').as_uri()\nfailures = []\ncount = 0\n\ndef check(name, okay, detail=''):\n    global count\n    count += 1\n    if not okay:\n        failures.append(name + ': ' + str(detail))\n\nwith sync_playwright() as p:\n    browser = p.chromium.launch(headless=True)\n    page = browser.new_page(viewport={'width': 1920, 'height': 1080})\n    errors = []\n    page.on('pageerror', lambda e: errors.append(str(e)))\n    page.goto(url)\n    page.wait_for_function('\"'!!window.TB?.app'\"')\n    page.wait_for_timeout(300)\n    check('export title identity', page.title() == 'Turtley Booked')\n    check('engine is foundation', page.evaluate('\"'!!TB.app.game.input && !!TB.app.game.audio && TB.app.game.view.id === \"overhead\"'\"'))\n    page.screenshot(path=str(root / 'build/title-tv.png'))\n    page.get_by_role('button', name='Check in • Solo', exact=True).click()\n    page.wait_for_timeout(2300)\n    check('solo starts production world', page.evaluate('TB.app.run.phase === \\\"playing\\\"'))\n    check('music gain default', page.evaluate('TB.app.game.settings.music === .1 && TB.app.game.audio.musicVolume === .1'))\n    page.screenshot(path=str(root / 'build/play-tv.png'))\n    page.keyboard.press('Escape')\n    page.wait_for_timeout(150)\n    check('native pause', page.evaluate('TB.app.game.paused && TB.app.ui.screen === \\\"pause\\\"'))\n    page.get_by_role('button', name='Developer tools', exact=True).click()\n    check('dev screen', page.get_by_role('heading', name='The caretaker’s cupboard').count() == 1)\n    page.get_by_role('button', name='Balance sliders', exact=True).click()\n    check('live sliders', page.locator('.esh input[type=range]').count() == 8)\n    page.screenshot(path=str(root / 'build/dev-tv.png'))\n    check('no runtime or draw errors', not errors and page.evaluate('TB.app.game.errors.length') == 0, errors or page.evaluate('TB.app.game.errors'))\n    browser.close()\nprint(json.dumps({'count': count, 'failures': failures}))\nsys.exit(1 if failures else 0)\nPY\ncat > tools/verify.mjs <<'JS'\nimport {spawnSync} from 'node:child_process';\nimport path from 'node:path';\nprocess.chdir(path.resolve(import.meta.dirname,'..'));\nconst suites=process.argv.slice(2);let count=0,failed=0;\nconst jobs=[];\nif(\"'!suites.length||suites.includes('\"'browser'))jobs.push(['/home/micha/.local/share/pipx/venvs/playwright/bin/python',['tests/browser.py']]);\nif(\"'!suites.length||suites.includes('\"'rules'))jobs.push(['node',['tests/rules.mjs']]);\nif(suites.includes('hub'))jobs.push(['/home/micha/.local/share/pipx/venvs/playwright/bin/python',['tests/hub.py']]);\nfor(const [cmd,args] of jobs){const r=spawnSync(cmd,args,{encoding:'utf8',maxBuffer:2e6});const lines=r.stdout.trim().split('\\\\n');let report;try{report=JSON.parse(lines.at(-1));}catch{report={count:0,failures:[r.stdout+r.stderr]};}count+=report.count;failed+=report.failures.length;for(const f of report.failures)console.error('FAIL '+f);if(r.status&&\"'!report.failures.length){failed++;console.error(r.stderr||'\"'Suite failed');}}\nconsole.log(\"'`${count} checks, ${failed} failures.`);process.exitCode=failed?1:0;\nJS\nnpm run verify -- browser'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_43","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> PROGRESS.md <<'MD'\n\n## Implementation checkpoint\n- All development is in \"'`Turtley-Booked-Turtles-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261106-033015/`.\n- Pinned full engine and unmodified Hub client/harness downloaded. Source manual and documented gameplay screenshot inspected; honest research record in `docs/research.md` (no footage/audio observed).\n- Read engine README, full API in chunks, relevant guide/index, assets card, arcade maze slice/GridMover, native Shell/settings/input/Blob/audio/headless example, Hub protocol/shared-world example/harness.\n- Implemented `src/content.js` (five authored connected floors), `sim.js` (deterministic native-grid rules, 26 rescues, all enemy states/bombs/damage/supply/transitions; snapshots; input-driven bots), `art.js` (custom native Blob-derived turtle/beetle continuous rigs and hotel map/title), `audio.js` (native synth/music/voice), `net.js` (authoritative shared-world protocol/dedicated host), `main.js` (native Shell screens/settings/pause/dev/local input), `style.css`.\n- Packager `npm run build` writes staged `build/game.html` and exact root delivery HTML; no external runtime assets. Root exit-interview.json still needs final factual content; provisional credits will be replaced by packager.\n- Exploratory production bot solo seed 2701 completed all five floors, 26 rescued, 415 simulated seconds, 2 hits, 24 plants, 18 triggers, 13 refills, 35 escalations. Co-op seed 2701 lost on roof at 23 rescued; improve bot tactics / validate other seeds before final claims.\n- Single command test orchestrator `npm run verify -- [browser|rules|hub]`. Initial browser smoke running; tests/rules.mjs and tests/hub.py not yet written.\n- Important unfinished verification: real final file visual/input/audio, actual Hub harness scenarios and synchronized full campaign, broader rules/races/objective integrity, touch/controller emulation, attract coverage and storage; documents and interview.\n- Do not inspect neighbors or kill other processes. Browser instances must close. No server started yet. Tools sessions may be running from verification.\nMD'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
