{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_84","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > tools/interview.mjs <<'JS'\nimport fs from 'node:fs';\nconst data={\n sourceInformation:{\n  date:'2026-11-06 03:30:15',source:'Turtles (1983 US Odyssey² hotel-rescue release; arcade ancestor 1981)',plan:'PLAN.md',genre:'Rescue-maze arcade action',perspective:'Fixed overhead 2D gameplay; illustrated hotel and rooftop intermissions',\n  tech:'JavaScript, self-contained HTML, my-3D2dge v0.89.1 (8ecc2f62353761187bdfe226f327b7ea5d2eb691), AI Hub protocol 1/client 1.4.0 (35a1047f2067b2af3de3943f0fe452f39105d869)',\n  artDirection:'Original shaded native pixel turtles, hatchlings, beetles and a warm miniature hotel; native props and lighting',animation:'Native continuous Blob-derived custom rigs, timers, easing, sorted pixel parts and particles',\n  audio:'Original code-only Web Audio/native synthesis: buoyant layered tune, distinct effects and formant gibberish; music defaults to 0.10; no audio files or TTS',\n  online:'AI Hub authoritative shared-world 1–2 player campaign with dedicated host support; standalone solo and simultaneous local co-op',\n  testing:'Native fixed-step rules and ordinary full campaigns, exact-file browser playback, standard gamepad stubs, Chromium CDP multitouch, WebKit phone profile, OfflineAudioContext, supplied multi-copy Hub harness with latency/jitter/loss and dedicated host, export/schema checks; no performance target',\n  research:'Read 1983 US manual and inspected its pictures and a documented gameplay screenshot; release entry and historical review cross-checked mechanics, progression, enemies, visuals and written sound descriptions. No original video or audio was watched/heard.',\n  environment:'Codex CLI (headless); Linux (Ubuntu on WSL2)',model:'OpenAI, gpt-6.1-sol, reasoning effort max',usage:'added on import'\n },\n testingFeedback:[\n  'Six unique product issues, all fixed; legitimate bot losses and automation-driver mistakes are recorded separately.',\n  'Two critical issues: an initial boot syntax error and a Hub-only presentation update error.',\n  'The complete bundled-game campaign through the actual Hub harness exposed a session-only update error missed by isolated rules tests.',\n  'Page-load-only smoke checks provided the least confidence about real progress and synchronization.'\n ],\n engineFeedback:[\n  'The native fixed-step loop, grid navigation, shaded pixel renderer and continuous rigs worked together without runtime dependencies.',\n  'Yes: TV scaling option placement and contextual touch-button creation required source inspection; signatures were checked against the pinned handoff.',\n  'The deterministic simultaneous-coop rescue simulation, especially passenger/home reservations and authoritative shared-world replication.',\n  'Keeping native UI/device handling and the online host lifetime consistent while sharing one simulation across all modes.',\n  'None. Game code extends native GridMover for immediate reversal and Blob for bespoke turtle and beetle anatomy.',\n  'Add a compact simultaneous shared-world kit demonstrating explicit input seats, lifecycle and snapshot reconciliation.'\n ],\n promptFeedback:[\n  'The manual-backed rescue relationships and concrete completion gates made the game coherent.',\n  'The year alone was ambiguous across ports; I explicitly used the 1983 US Odyssey² release.',\n  'Verifying a complete cooperative campaign and device/lifecycle behavior in one self-contained HTML.',\n  'Separate mandatory acceptance checks from suggested tuning values, and supply one minimal engine/shared-world integration example.'\n ],\n aiHub:{name:'Turtley Booked',tagline:'Small shells. Big room service.',description:'Give 26 tiny hotel guests a lift home across five mischievous maze floors. Outwit maturing beetles, share a scarce bug bomb, and reunite the family on the roof, solo or with a friend.',type:'Game',genre:'Action',source:'Turtles (1983 US Odyssey²)',series:'',players:'1–2',controls:'Stick/D-pad or WASD/arrows move; Cross/Space bombs; click routes/right-click bombs; co-op WASD/Space + arrows/Right Shift; touch drag + contextual POP.',tags:['2d','arcade','co-op','top-down','pixel art','comedy']}\n};fs.writeFileSync('../exit-interview.json',JSON.stringify(data,null,2)+'\\\\n');\nJS\nnode tools/interview.mjs\ncat > README.md <<'MD'\n# Turtley Booked\n\n**Small shells. Big room service.** An original rescue-maze arcade game: five floors, 26 hatchlings, one shared defensive bomb and a rooftop family evacuation.\n\nOpen the containing folder's \"'`Turtley-Booked-Turtles-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261106-033015.html` directly in a browser. No server, install, CDN, images or audio files are needed for standalone play. AI Hub supplies remote shared-world sessions; the file itself supplies solo and simultaneous local co-op.\n\n- Solo: WASD or arrows; Space bombs. Mouse click routes; right click bombs.\n- Standard pad: stick/D-pad; Cross bombs; Options pauses. PlayStation glyphs default, Xbox optional.\n- Shared keyboard: WASD/Space and arrows/Right Shift. Mixed keyboard/pad and two-pad seats are explicit menu choices.\n- Touch: invisible four-way drag stick, contextual POP and optional assisted auto-defence. Single-device touch is solo.\n\nNative pause has Settings, Controls, Developer tools and About/Credits. Developer balance/cheats mark practice; solo, co-op, assisted and practice records are separate. In Hub, pause is local and production tools are read-only. An explicit `dev=1` query allows authoritative tools on a test host.\n\nBuild: `npm run --silent build`. Verify: `npm run --silent verify`. Optional suite names follow `--` (rules, browser, devices, audio, network, hub, hub-campaign, export). Tests reuse installed Python Playwright; no browser installation is required. The Hub tests bind temporary loopback OS-assigned ports and stop only their own servers.\n\nSee `docs/research.md`, `docs/authoring.md`, `docs/validation.md` and `docs/provenance.md`. Root `exit-interview.json` is the source for the embedded About feedback/catalogue information. The pinned full engine and unmodified Hub client are in vendor.\nMD\npython3 - <<'\"'PY'\np='tools/verify.mjs';s=open(p).read().replace(\\\"if(suites.includes('hub-campaign'))\\\", \\\"if(\"'!suites.length||suites.includes('\"'export'))jobs.push(['node',['tests/export.mjs']]);\\\\nif(\"'!suites.length||suites.includes('\"'hub-campaign'))\\\").replace(\\\"if(suites.includes('hub'))\\\", \\\"if(\"'!suites.length||suites.includes('\"'hub'))\\\");open(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\nbiome check --write src tools tests/*.mjs --diagnostic-level=error > build/biome.log 2>&1 || true\nnpm run --silent build && npm run --silent verify -- rules devices audio network export\"","aggregated_output":"Built Turtley-Booked-Turtles-gpt-6.1-sol-max-20261106-033015.html (1393564 bytes)\nFAIL 'NoneType' object is not subscriptable\n131 checks, 1 failures.\n","exit_code":1,"status":"failed"}}
